DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     This translates a vnode into its component name, and writes that name to
     the head of the buffer specified by _b_u_f.

     _v_p      The vnode to translate.

     _d_v_p     The vnode of the parent directory of _v_p.

     _c_r_e_d    The caller credentials.

     _b_u_f     The buffer into which to prepend the component name.

     _b_u_f_l_e_n  The remaining size of the buffer.

     The default implementation of VVOOPP__VVPPTTOOCCNNPP scans through _v_p's parent di‐
     rectory looking for a dirent with a matching file number.  If _v_p is not a
     directory, then VVOOPP__VVPPTTOOCCNNPP returns ENOENT.

LLOOCCKKSS
     The vnode should be locked on entry and will still be locked on exit.
     The parent directory vnode will be unlocked on a successful exit.  How‐
     ever, it will have its use count incremented.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     Zero is returned on success, otherwise an error code is returned.

EERRRROORRSS
     [ENOMEM]           The buffer was not large enough to hold the vnode's
                        component name.

     [ENOENT]           The vnode was not found on the file system.

